## Interface: 16001, 120105
## Title: Navigation
## Notes: Sane UI's minimap and map in one window. Small in the screen's top right corner it is the minimap; move the mouse into that corner and it fills the screen as the map. Drag it, zoom it with the mouse wheel from a zone out to the whole world, right click for one map out, a click pings the place to your group, a double click puts the map pin there; draw it as Parchment (Blizzard's maps joined into one) or as Scrying (the land as it lies). Pins of your quests, flight points, rares, places and party; the maps of the dungeons and raids; the quest log over the full map, pinned to the screen if you like; a golden line to the map pin, on foot and by flight. The game's map keys open it. Settings: the page Navigation.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Map_01
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table, its settings and the command. First: the other files add to that table.
Navigation.lua
# The map's spaces (map, world, the plane it is drawn in), the map tree, the terrain's grid. Knows no frames
Coords.lua
# Where a view looks: its middle, its zoom, following the player, the map its zoom shows. Knows no frames
Camera.lua
# Retail's map: the game's own map tree, one map at a time (a Retail-only override of the camera and two answers of the map tree)
Camera.Retail.lua
# What the game tells while playing: the player, the map pin, group, quests, flights, rares, explored areas. Knows no frames
Live.lua
# The game's minimap ping on our map: a click pings a place to the group, their pings shown where they are. No frames
Ping.lua
# The pins as plain records: the game's and Core's data, one per thing, filtered, gathered. Knows no frames
Pins.lua
# What your quests still ask of the world and where exactly it stands, from Core's data. Knows no frames
Goals.lua
# Herbs and ore: what one is by its name, its picture, the game's finders switched silently and in turn. Knows no frames
Nodes.lua
# Where a player can walk: Core's walking data, unpacked per tile when first needed. Knows no frames
Walk.lua
# The walking data's coarse layer: each tile's gates into the next, what the walks between them cost. Knows no frames
Gates.lua
# A walk between two points over the walking data, as a job of Core's scheduler. Knows no frames
Search.lua
# The lifts on the walking data: each end at its landing, the levels they join, where a place stands. Knows no frames
Lifts.lua
# The way to the map pin: on foot, by the flights this character knows, by ship, tram and lift. Knows no frames
Planner.lua
# While you are dead: the map pin at your corpse, the one you had back once you live again. Knows no frames
Corpse.lua
# At a flight master: our full map in place of the game's flight map (Shift: the game's), its flight points to click
Taxi.lua
# The frame the map is drawn in, the same for both views: its layers, the player's place, the mouse
Canvas.lua
# The terrain: the game's minimap textures up close, the module's overview of them further out
Terrain.lua
# The zones that have an outline to cut their map art to (made by dev/tools/terrain-art, not by hand): Forever's world
Outlines.lua [ExcludeLoadGameType standard]
# The tiles on a coast, cut by a finer mask of their own up close (made by dev/tools/terrain-art, not by hand): Forever's
Coasts.lua [ExcludeLoadGameType standard]
# Blizzard's map art: the world's, the continent's, the zones' cut to their outlines, and the explored parts
Art.lua
# The zone under the mouse named over the full map, as the game's map does: its name, levels and fishing skill
Label.lua
# The indoor map of the building you are in: the game's indoor pictures without their black, at your floor
Indoors.lua
# A quest's areas, as the game shades them, over each zone in view
Areas.lua
# The maps of the dungeons and raids, chosen in the bar: over the map in its place, by floor
Dungeons.lua
# The golden line of the way to the map pin: its pulse (the game makes that animation only from XML), its lines
Route.xml
Route.lua
# The ways of the flight point or dock under the mouse: its flights white, a ship's way round light blue
Paths.lua
# The pins drawn: a button each, in the game's own looks
PinView.lua
# The Sane Rare tracker: a rare, a treasure or an event near you told at once, by a notice on the screen and a horn
RareTracker.lua
# Over the map at a fixed size: the party, the player's arrow, the map pin
Marks.lua
# The game's minimap over ours, for its live dots; taken and given back
Hybrid.lua
# The herbs and ore the game's minimap shows, found by asking it and drawn over it in their own pictures
Found.lua
# Gold sparkles in the world on the herb or ore your interact key would gather
Sparkles.lua
Glints.lua
# Other addons' buttons from round the game's minimap and the addons of its compartment, held for the satchel
Strays.lua
# The satchel: a button on the small map opening a page of the addons' buttons, the pins and the game's tracking
Satchel.lua
# The satchel's line of Core's sound profiles: the profile in use, the game's sound settings under a cogwheel
AudioLine.lua
# The game's map kept closed: its keys and every way to it open ours
Native.lua
# The quest log, a window of its own over the full map; pinned, on the screen while the map is small too
QuestLog.lua
# At a dock: where its boats and zeppelins go and when they come, at the top of the screen
DockWatch.lua
# The trip you are on, at the top of the screen: where it goes, how far, how long; on a flight, Request Stop
TripView.lua
# The bar over the full map: the quest log, the views, the map selector, the dungeons, the pin filter
TopBar.lua
# The window: the minimap in the top right corner, the map when it fills the screen
Window.lua
